module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unsolved_placeholder_reads_back_as_unit

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unsolved_placeholder_reads_back_as_unit: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unsolved_placeholder_reads_back_as_unit" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an element whose type is an UNSOLVED inference placeholder reaches a consumer typed as the concrete kernel type Unit. v1.compiler.infer types an empty list literal with no expected type as List of type_variable_node empty_list_element. When nothing later solves that variable, an element read from the list arrives at field access as Unit, and the refusal names Unit as the type. The value's type was never established, and the diagnostic reports a type it does not have.",

    "SPECIMEN, executed 2026-10-05 with gunbc built at main ed68b5573b (gunbc run, a fixture module outside the corpus): `let modules = fold_list(xs: ms(), empty: [], cons: fn(acc, m) { acc })` with ms() returning List<UMod>, then `match modules |> first { Present { value: m } => m.module  Absent => `` }`, refuses `no field 'module' on type 'Unit'`. The same read with a list built by `list_snoc_item(xs: [], item: ..)` instead refuses with the typed message that names the real state: the scrutinee's type is unresolved, give the value a declared type. One unsolved variable, two diagnostics; only the second is true.",

    "HARM: fabricated plausible output in a diagnostic (DESIGN section 5). The refusal is loud and located, so no wrong program is accepted, but it names a type the program never had. It sends the reader after a Unit-producing bug that does not exist. Measured cost, 2026-10-05: on gunbc#13330 a reader spent two falsified repair rounds (child_type_node narrowing; a first-come placeholder rule) before subtraction located the real cause. That cause was an accumulator never solved because v1.compiler.infer unify_generics does not descend a callable's return.",

    "PRODUCER, located 2026-10-06 on gunbc#13475: v1.compiler.infer ExprListLit, empty literal, expected Present but not an element collection. fold_list's empty: [] is inferred against the accumulator generic A, so expected is Present; A is not a collection, and the arm answered unit_type. unify_generics then bound A to List<Unit> (an informative node) and never overrode it from cons. Field access on an element of that list therefore named Unit.",

    "CLIMB, gunbc#13475: the Present-non-collection arm now mints type_variable_node empty_list_element, the same unknown the no-expected arm already used. unify_generics binds that uninformative list and unify_lambda_solves overrides it from an informing cons. unify_callable_generics is the callable descent (params and return) the 2026-10-05 cause named; collection_fold_roles only chooses the step's expected type so xs can inform T without child_type_node erasing a TypeVariable slot (piece 2 / #13330). List append (concat or +) takes an informative right list when the left is still the placeholder, so language fold(init: []) whose step is concat(acc, [x]) produces List of the appended element. When every actual is uninformative, declared-return conformance TypeMismatches a ground declared type against the unsolved produced generic. The call-argument grain of unbound_generic_reaches_conformance_unjudged (p7b) is still piece 3.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (loud, located, misattributed). CLIMBED ON #13475 to mechanically preventable for the Unit-fabrication arm and the identity-cons declared-return admission this skip opened. CEILING: 3 -- an unsolved placeholder is a modeled state (TypeVariable), so every reader can refuse it as unresolved instead of substituting a concrete type. NEXT TRIGGER: piece 3, the remaining call-argument grain of unbound_generic_reaches_conformance_unjudged (p7b) — an unresolved generic reaching a direct-call argument refuses cannot infer; annotate.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
